// A generic function cannot be a callback: a vtable slot holds one code
// address and a generic function has one per instantiation. That is the same
// reason an interface cannot declare a generic method. The workaround is an
// instantiating wrapper, which the message names.
interface Count { int of(List<int> xs); }
int firstof<T>(List<T> xs) { return xs.size(); }
Count c = firstof;
print(c.of([1, 2]));
